WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.910
The Digital World,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.050
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.470
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.300
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.070
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.710
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.490
The evil Whispered used 
Apollomon as a shield

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.280
and tried to take away my will to fight.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.330
But when I realized that 
my reluctance to attack

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.460
was putting my friends in danger 
and even hurting Apollomon,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.170
I made the decision to endure 
the pain and defeat him.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.950
X7's attack destroyed Whispered 
along with Apollomon,

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:20.270
and we succeeded at last in defeating 
all seven Death Generals.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:32.280
<b>Reborn!</b>

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:32.280
<b>All Seven Death Generals Appear!!</b>

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:30.660
Reborn! All Seven Death Generals Appear!!

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.630
So that's the Bagra Army's home 
base, the Great Bagra Palace?

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.910
And of course, Bagramon...

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.020
...is inside.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.840
Yeah. If we eliminate Bagramon,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.570
the Digital World can be reborn.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.070
And the friends we've lost 
will come back to us.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.130
Like Beelzebumon!

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.900
And Deckerdramon.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.470
Not just them.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.640
There's also Apollomon, and all the others 
who placed their hope in us before dying.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.940
We've worked hard to come this far, 
with that dream on our minds.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.240
Yeah. Let's go.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.750
There's nobody here.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.300
Yeah... it's so quiet.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.020
Too quiet.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.290
That just makes me suspicious.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.390
We made it to the entrance.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.450
A trap?

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.530
It must be.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.250
What should we do, Taiki?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.280
Let's go.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.820
B-Bagramon!

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.720
That's...

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.860
...the Emperor of the Bagra Empire...

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.760
...Bagramon?

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:08.790
Welcome, Generals.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.580
You have done well to come this 
far with so few in number.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.830
I commend you.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.590
You creep! C'mon and fight!

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.840
No... something doesn't feel right...

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.010
The Palace is...

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.010
You're...

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.180
DarkKnightmon!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.520
What are you playing at?!

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.070
You are not pleased?

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.700
This is only a game...

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.310
the kind Yuu loves so much.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.680
Where have you taken Yuu?!

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.760
Give him back to me!

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:20.130
If you wish to see Yuu, 
I can arrange it right now...

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:27.040
If all of you, including 
Taiki Kudou, bow before me.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.540
What?!

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.160
I'm saying that if you surrender 
and become my minions,

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.450
all of this will be resolved.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:38.130
DarkKnightmon, you seem to be 
the type that forgets easily,

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.050
so make sure you remember this very well.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.250
Oh?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.910
We will never give in 
to bad guys like you!

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.330
Yeah! That's what Xros 
Heart is all about!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.860
And we are all bound by 
our powerful friendship!

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.090
That's too bad.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.640
Then allow me to show you a miracle.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.700
A miracle?

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.310
As I'm sure you've all noticed,

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:07.610
we gather Digimon's pain, 
suffering, anger, and hatred,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:13.770
and store the negative energy born from 
these feelings within the Code Crown.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:19.640
That negative energy has 
reformed the Code Crown

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:24.330
into a Dark Stone filled with dark power.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.100
The Code Crown is...

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.310
Here it is.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:36.310
The Dark Stone, created for the 
approaching day of destruction, D5.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.080
I will show you a bit of its power.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:45.090
Return to life, Death Generals!

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:05.970
What is this?!

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.380
Come forth, Death Generals!

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:18.280
The Fire Fury, Dorbickmon.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:22.900
The Moon Light, NeoVamdemon.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.720
The Wood Spirit, Zamielmon.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.830
The Water Tiger, Splashmon.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.070
The Gold Thief, Olegmon.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.920
The Earth God, Gravimon.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.480
The Sun Wheel, Apollomon.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.080
All the Death Generals...

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.210
...have come back to life!

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:57.120
It can't be...

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.180
The Digital World hasn't 
even been reborn yet!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.160
How can you do that?!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:06.860
That is one of the miracles 
of the Dark Stone.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.090
Get them!

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.870
Olegmon! Don't do this!

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.630
Didn't you say Taiki won you over,

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.510
and even wish him good luck?!

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:22.510
And I thought Apollomon was 
freed from Whispered in the end!

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.550
Apollomon! Olegmon! Say something!

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.380
It's no use.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:32.590
Your voices won't reach them.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.160
We won't know that until we try!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.900
You're wasting your time. 
They have no souls.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.800
No souls?

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:47.500
It was because they had souls 
that we met with such insolence

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.510
as Apollomon awakening to justice.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:56.050
Cold-hearted warriors who only heed 
my orders have no need for souls.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.750
You can't mean...

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.880
You took away their souls by force?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.650
Is there a problem with that?

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.280
That's too cruel!

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:04.290
I won't forgive you!

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.000
Taiki, Nene! Let's go!

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.880
Yeah!

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:07.830
Yes!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.390
Reload!

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.900
Greymon!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.930
MailBirdramon!

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.000
DigiXros!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.110
MetalGreymon!

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.590
Let's do it, everyone!

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.610
Great Xros!

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.330
Shoutmon!

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.850
MetalGreymon!

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:31.870
Digivolve!

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.520
OmegaShoutmon!

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.840
ZekeGreymon!

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.320
Ballistamon!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.660
Dorulumon!

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:42.360
Starmons!

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.770
Yes!

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:45.750
Sparrowmon!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.030
Great Xros!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:11.600
Shoutmon X7!

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.090
Feel the power of warriors without souls!

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:18.730
Get them!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:21.730
Turbulence Arrow!

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.540
Gardiac Raid!

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.390
Dragon Breath Tonic Fire!

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.810
Arrow of Apollo!

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.010
Octa Gravity!

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.700
Repel them with Xros Burning Rocker!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.400
Xros Burning Rocker!

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.070
As expected.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:55.100
But can you defeat this Digimon?

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:58.770
All Death Generals, DigiXros!

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:17.290
All the Death Generals 
have combined into one!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.620
It's so huge...

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.050
The time has come to reveal the power

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.800
of the strongest and most evil god 
of destruction, GrandGeneramon!

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:32.840
We won't lose!

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.610
Double Flare Buster!

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:37.420
Double Flare Buster!

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.840
Shoutmon X7!

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.440
Everyone!

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:01.410
Are you okay?!

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:02.430
Darn it...

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:07.040
You're finished, Shoutmon.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.250
Shoutmon!

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.060
Hey, Shoutmon! Get a hold of yourself!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.890
What did you do to Shoutmon?!

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.780
<b>"Original Digimon Contest" The Five Special Award Winners</b>

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.780
1. The Taiki and Shoutmon Award

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.780
<b>Chicchi's Design</b>

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.780
<b>Ekakimon</b>

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.340
What did you do to Shoutmon?!

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:42.970
Just like the Death Generals,

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.380
I've stolen his soul.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:46.040
What?!

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:49.800
Digimon who have been corrupted 
by that virus known as justice

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.510
have no value to me as servants.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:56.200
It's best to abandon them 
by the wayside like garbage.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.860
You monster...

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.790
DarkKnightmon, give Shoutmon's soul back!

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.960
It's your turn next, Taiki Kudou.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:08.630
I'll seal you away in the 
prison of souls, Prison Land!

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:11.420
No!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.780
Dorulumon! You've gotta hang in there!

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.350
Taiki, we have to withdraw!

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.380
Get on MailBirdramon!

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:24.790
Greymon, return!

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.430
Taiki!

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.120
Don't worry about Shoutmon and Dorulumon!

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.520
We'll carry them!

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.760
Take care of them!

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.760
It's no use.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.460
Taiki!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:36.590
Ballistamon!

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.070
Let's go, MailBirdramon!

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:46.750
Now, wait a minute!

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.240
Go on, run away.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.850
That's where the real fun begins.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.370
This is a true hunter's game.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.390
I'm going to enjoy this.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.970
We managed to escape behind a crag,

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.730
but he'll find us in a heartbeat here.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:12.000
You can't return them 
to your Xros Loader?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.900
No... I tried, but...

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.900
It's probably because 
their souls are gone.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.330
Hang tight, guys.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.800
I swear I'll get your souls back.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:27.020
And Apollomon's and 
Olegmon's along with them.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:28.950
They're Death Generals!

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:32.940
But Olegmon knew how to care 
for his friends, didn't he?

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:36.160
And before Whispered took control of him,

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.620
Apollomon had a just heart!

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.520
But they probably have 
evil hearts, as well.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.490
We don't know whether they'll 
take the side of good or evil.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.090
I want to believe in them!

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:50.030
You never change.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.670
But how can we get their souls back?

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.340
That's what I can't figure out.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:59.210
When I was absorbed by NeoVamdemon,

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.740
I was saved by Shoutmon.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:07.320
He intentionally got himself 
absorbed by NeoVamdemon

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.850
and came after me.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:12.840
That's it! So that's how!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.190
Taiki, what are you planning to do?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.110
You can't mean...

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:20.820
I do.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:24.150
I'll let him take my soul, 
then go to Prison Land

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.100
and bring back the souls of 
Shoutmon and the others.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:28.620
You can't! Humans aren't like Digimon!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.100
He's right! Something is bound to happen

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.680
if a human's soul is sent 
back and forth like that!

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:37.470
No, if Digimon can do it, 
I'm sure humans can, too.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.910
Wisemon, what do you think?

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:42.920
You do have a point.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.420
Just like Digimon are 
powered by digital signals,

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.980
humans are powered by electrical 
signals in the brain.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:53.910
Which may mean that humans 
and Digimon are very similar.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.670
I don't really understand the hard stuff,

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:59.840
but I believe that humans 
and Digimon are the same.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.050
Taiki...

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.960
It's just like you to think that.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.650
I'm kinda happy to hear that!

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.010
Taiki Kudou.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.780
I have you all completely surrounded.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.980
Will you still insist on fighting?

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.370
Or will you surrender?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.160
I will give you some time 
to make your choice.

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:24.260
I'm going.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.120
It's our only choice now.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.050
No. If you go, so will I.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.020
Me, too.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:30.740
And me!

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:32.110
And me!

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:33.470
And us!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:34.740
Wait a minute, guys...

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:37.420
Something feels dangerous 
about that Prison Land

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.610
where stolen souls are sent.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.310
That's why we should go with you!

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.850
We don't know what 
DarkKnightmon will do

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.850
while my soul is removed from me.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:50.070
I want you to protect the 
others while I'm gone, Kiriha.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:50.760
Me?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.990
Yes. And if I mess this up...

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.610
Take care of them all.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:16:59.880
All right.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.960
But you'd better come back!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.470
I won't tolerate failure!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.880
You're harsh, as always.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.920
I got it. I promise I'll come back.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.360
Taiki! We believe in you!

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.310
We're rooting for you!

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:22.690
Time's up.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.590
Taiki Kudou.

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:28.760
DarkKnightmon...

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.900
Will it be battle or surrender?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:32.960
Neither.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.070
Oh? Then what?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.140
I'll go to Prison Land, 
just like you wanted.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:43.370
I'll go to Prison Land and bring 
Shoutmon and my other friends back.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.010
I see.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:48.250
And you really think you can do that?

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.590
I don't know.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.750
But I don't want to be separated 
from my friends like this forever!

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:58.980
You are the brilliant General 
who defeated Yuu.

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:03.630
However, no one has ever returned 
from Prison Land before.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.560
But I still want to go!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.500
Interesting.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:11.890
I am most eager to see whether you 
can make it back from Prison Land.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.440
Are you ready?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:15.510
Yes.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:20.850
Such courage for one who is 
about to have his soul stolen.

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.700
Taiki Kudou...

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:44.850
Prison Land will not be as 
forgiving as you expect.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:48.710
Go on and suffer.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.880
This is Prison Land?

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:34.540
It really does look like 
a prison of souls...

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:37.820
like a land that could rob 
you of all hopes and dreams.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:43.140
But still, the fact that I exist here

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.860
must mean that my soul 
really materialized?

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:49.130
Which means Shoutmon and the others 
must have materialized here, too!

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.500
All right,

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.190
I'll find you right away!

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:54.640
You are naive, Taiki Kudou!

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.140
That voice...

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:01.450
Gravimon!

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:08.920
We Death Generals' souls have 
materialized here, just like yours did!

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.400
As you can see!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.770
NeoVamdemon!

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:14.990
Zamielmon!

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.970
Whispered!

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:18.330
Olegmon!

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:20.190
Splashmon!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.730
Dorbickmon!

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:25.230
Here, we can also act on our own will

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:28.150
and take vengeance on you!

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:30.710
Nothing could make us happier!

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:39.120
Taiki Kudou, what sort of battle will 
you show us in these circumstances?

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:43.120
Or will you fall to your knees 
and beg for forgiveness?

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.470
Gravimon, you seem to be the 
type that forgets easily, too,

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.410
so make sure you remember this very well!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.830
We...

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.030
We...

00:20:56.160 --> 00:21:00.000
will never give in to bad guys like you!

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.260
Shoutmon!

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.610
That's what Xros Heart is all about.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.740
Dorulumon!

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:11.780
Our hearts are bound by 
our powerful friendship!

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.690
Ballistamon!

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:14.850
Taiki!

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:18.460
Don't tell me you got your soul 
stolen so you could save us?!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:22.220
Yeah, and that's how I was 
able to come to Prison Land!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:24.100
You are as reckless as ever.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.500
But so passionate!

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:30.640
And that passion gave 
us all enormous power!

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:34.770
Yeah! That power is welling 
up from the depths of my soul!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:38.110
A hundred times the power, 
a thousand times the courage!

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:41.610
If this place is a prison for souls,

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.950
then let's take them on with 
the passion of our own souls!

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:46.750
Yeah! There's no way we can lose!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:49.150
Even if we're up against Death Generals!

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:51.430
We will win!

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:53.350
What nonsense!

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:56.760
If you can't become X7, 
you're no more than scum!

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.000
We'll kick you around like pebbles!

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:02.570
Okay, guys...

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:04.380
Let's do it!

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.540
Yeah!

